    "title": "UNC women's basketball locks in to beat Maryland in March Madness: Score, highlights",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 2:15 p.m. ETCHAPEL HILL — North Carolina women's basketball locked in down the stretch to defeat Maryland 74-66 in Carmichael Arena on Sunday, earning a second straight trip to the Sweet 16 where the Heels are likely to face No. 1 overall seed UConn.UNC (28-7) held Maryland (24-9) to its second-lowest scoring game of the season as sophomore guard Elina Aarnisalo poured in 21 points to lead the Tar Heels.Despite inspired play from former Duke guard Oluchi Okananwa, who led Maryland with 21 points, the Tar Heels executed cleanly down the stretch, capitalized by a Nyla Brooks 3-pointer that doubled UNC’s lead with 1:43 left to play, and a driving Lanie Grant layup that put the Heels up by eight.Up next for UNC is the winner of Monday’s No. 1 seed UConn vs. No. 9 Syracuse game in the Fort Worth 1 Regional. The Heels’ Sweet 16 matchup will be played Friday, March 27, in Dickies Arena.Watch the Women's NCAA Tournament on Fubo (free trial)UNC women's basketball vs Maryland in NCAA Tournament Final: UNC 74, Maryland 66UNC reaches a second straight Sweet 16 and is likely to face No. 1 UConn in Forth Worth on Friday.The Tar Heels' 28 wins are second-most of the Courtney Banghart era and they're going to back-to-back Sweet 16s for the first time in more than a decade. Heels holding onUNC is defending well and leaving the right shots for Maryland, which has hit only 3-of-19 attempts from 3-point range.The Terps are shooting 32% to UNC's 47% and they've missed 10 free throws. End of 3Q: UNC 50, Maryland 50Maryland outscores UNC 17-8 in the third quarter to pull even, ironically, from the foul line where the Terps have made just 13-of-23 (57%).Okananwa is playing like her season depends on it. She has 15 points, four O boards and two steals.Aarnisalo, who has a game-high 17 points for UNC, has picked up her fourth foul along with Nivar.Maryland has 23 FT attempts while UNC has been to the line just seven times. Under 5: UNC 48, Maryland 41UNC's young guard Lanie Grant pops a deep jumper to push UNC's lead back up to seven points.Grant has 11 points on 5-of-10 shooting. Still a teenager, Grant decided to forego her senior year of high school to join the Heels last season. Frese is ampedMaryland coach Brenda Frese was on the court hyping up her Terps after they forced a UNC timeout with a halfcourt trap.The Terps have cut it to 46-41 with 5:04 left in the half.Frese also appeared to challenge Okananwa on the bench with an intense pep talk. Okananwa responded with a bucket and the Terps have momentum. Nivar gets 4th foulUNC senior Indya Nivar gets foul No. 4 with 6:45 left in the third quarter. Halftime: UNC 42, Maryland 33Elina Aarnisalo scores her 13th point on a 3-pointer to close the half with UNC leading by nine.UNC has picked up the pace and it's shooting 57% while holding Maryland to 34%.The Heels also hold a 20-19 rebounding edge, they've locked in on defense and they're winning the battle in the paint 26-16. Heels off and runningUNC has doubled up the Terps, outscoring them 12-6 so far in the second quarter. Frese calls timeout and it's 34-23 UNC with 4:58 to go until halftime.End of 1Q: UNC 22, Maryland 17Elina Aarnisalo scores the Heels' first four points but the Terps led by as many as 6 before a 9-0 run put UNC back on top.What channel is UNC vs Maryland on today in NCAA Women's Tournament?TV Channel: ESPNLivestream: Fubo (free trial)UNC vs. Maryland in the NCAA Tournament second round will be televised nationally on ESPN. The game can be streamed on Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers.UNC vs Maryland start time in NCAA Women's Tournament bracket Date: Sunday, March 22Time: NoonThe UNC vs. Maryland game starts at noon ET from Carmichael Arena in Chapel Hill.",
